{"game": "elden-ring-nightreign", "language": "english", "appid": 2622380, "month": "2026-01", "window": 4, "start_date": 1769212800, "end_date": 1769903999, "month_true_total": 2580, "quota": 9, "returned": 9, "pulled_at": "2026-10-04 23:47:09 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "217293739", "author": {"steamid": "76561198079075069", "personaname": "Alger_Hiss", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Alger_Hiss/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 3, "playtime_forever": 2064, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 565, "last_played": 1787781925, "avatar": "bf3b8a76a7502570520ba57418aad3b823ac5851"}, "language": "english", "review": "I SUCK AND IT IS GOOD FRICKING DARK ELDEN FORTNITE\r\n\\", "timestamp_created": 1769899569, "timestamp_updated": 1769899569, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1748555952", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "217291782", "author": {"steamid": "76561198172460394", "personaname": "sheinhardtwigs", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198172460394/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 2, "playtime_forever": 5401, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1459, "last_played": 1789045435, "avatar": "b23d56198ef23e49161b7623f002bdd3ba9192a0"}, "language": "english", "review": "Base game is good but deep of night is ♥♥♥♥ and was obviously never playtested. The DLC is a barebones scam. Fromsoft managed to trash an awesome concept which is really surprising.", "timestamp_created": 1769897843, "timestamp_updated": 1769897843, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.478527605533599854", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1748555952", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "217291173", "author": {"steamid": "76561197963287051", "personaname": "Problem Machine", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/problemmachine/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 24, "playtime_forever": 12802, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 12220, "last_played": 1771728206, "avatar": "d98d97859bc530d1bf5ea1ef20781cfc81448702"}, "language": "english", "review": "A very cool experiment in game design, From treads new ground in the most efficient way possible, reusing large numbers of Elden Ring assets and reconfiguring them into a completely new experience. A little bit like a roguelike, a little bit like a battle royale, Nightreign has you racing against the clock trying to become as powerful as possible across two days before the showdown with the Nightlord on the third day. Defeating the challenge requires you to figure out a route through the semi-randomized map on the fly, avoiding powerful enemies until you've leveled up, hunting down ruins holding weapons with the boss's weakness, deciding whether you're better off going to a mine to upgrade your weapon or going to a high level fight to hope a better weapon drops. Each playable character is similar to a build you might create for an Elden Ring playthrough, but with a set of unique skills and passives that suit that role -- The dedicated caster has an ability that lets her recover spellpower and concoct new spells based on elemental residue, the greatsword warrior has a grappling hook that lets him quickly move in and out of combat range, the hulking tank has an ability that lets him briefly ignore damage and create a massive counterattack. Each character feels very distinctive, much more so than an Elden Ring playthrough, and having to improvise with what you find gives an opportunity to experiment with weapons and spells you'd never touch on such a playthrough. It's not for everyone, the relentless pace can be difficult to get used to, but I think this experiment is a resounding success.", "timestamp_created": 1769897287, "timestamp_updated": 1769897287, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 9, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.616151988506317139", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1748555952", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "217290205", "author": {"steamid": "76561198101359642", "personaname": "Kiraneko", "persona_status": "in-game", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Nekoking69/", "num_games_owned": 565, "num_reviews": 146, "playtime_forever": 6304, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 6131, "last_played": 1780863910, "avatar": "b8d47024f23209dabf183245361bc897a1c5891a"}, "language": "english", "review": "More fun multiplayer experience for people who played and enjoyed elden ring, but with less depth, its good for what it is, but for me personally even though I like the gameplay, it being non cannon makes it harder for me to invest in it.", "timestamp_created": 1769896481, "timestamp_updated": 1769896481, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1748555952", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "217289744", "author": {"steamid": "76561199072652101", "personaname": "Bingus", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/BingusTheNimrod/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 28, "playtime_forever": 1727, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1572, "last_played": 1769979825, "avatar": "4dadafc94d05a73fd743167a25239af78c6a591a"}